      "writtenOn": "2026-06-23T15:54:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If clients can redefine SkLog, then they may lose the ability to notify the log handler (if they don\u0027t realize they have to invoke it).\n\nShould we just say clients that want to collect log messages are expected to override SkLog? Or if we think SkLogHandler provides a better way to let client\u0027s abstract their logs, then maybe SkLog isn\u0027t a macro at all and can\u0027t be overridden in that manner.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 14,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 14,
        "endChar": 62
      },
      "revId": "4dee2f1f31c1301ddaa817bb7501de14c0200ad2",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
